  "notes": "{朗読|ろうどく} is a noun that also functions as a suru-verb ({朗読|ろうどく}する). It implies reading with expression and projection, not simply reading text out loud.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {詩|し}を{朗読|ろうどく}する (to recite a poem)\n- {朗読|ろうどく}する (to read aloud)\n- {朗読|ろうどく}{会|かい} (a reading/recitation event)\n- {朗読|ろうどく}ボランティア (volunteer reader)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{音読|おんどく} is reading aloud for practice or study (often in classrooms), while {朗読|ろうどく} implies a more polished, performative reading with attention to expression and delivery. {黙読|もくどく} is silent reading.",
